# --------------------------------------------------------------- results ---
# Generated output. Regenerate with:
#     python scripts/reproduce.py --profile paper
# Provenance is recorded in results/<profile>/metadata/provenance.json, so these
# files are reconstructible rather than primary sources.
# Written as results/* rather than results/ so that a single subdirectory can be
# re-included below; git will not descend into a directory ignored by name.
results/*

# Exception: the hardware measurements are primary data, not generated output.
# A simulator result can be rebuilt by running the script again; a device run
# cannot be rebuilt at all -- it cost QPU time, the calibration it was taken
# under is gone, and the same job will never return the same counts.
!results/hardware/

# ----------------------------------------------------------- credentials ---
# API tokens and account files never belong in the repository. The hardware
# script reads IBM_QUANTUM_TOKEN from the environment for exactly this reason.
.qiskit/
qiskit-ibm.json
qiskit-ibm-runtime.json
*credentials*.json
secrets.*
*.token
*_token.txt
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.netrc

